    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "The `butler-capture` crate: a `ScreenSource` trait that yields one `Frame` of one monitor on demand, an `xcap`-backed implementation for Windows and macOS, monitor enumeration and selection, and the `Frame` type whose lifecycle rules (in-memory only, no `Serialize`, dropped after recognition) are the first link in the privacy chain. Snapshot polling at a configurable interval replaces continuous video capture: the pipeline asks for a frame when the state machine says so, never on a free-running loop. Cadence, scheduling and backoff are the state machine's (009); this crate only knows how to take one picture.\n",
    "title": "Screen capture: snapshot polling of one monitor through the compositor"
